{"type":"definition","type_name":"Definition","number":"1.2.2","title":"Bounded Sets","title_html":"Bounded Sets","html":"<p>Let <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"F\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> be an ordered field and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"A \\subseteq F\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2286\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. The set <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"A\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is <strong>bounded above</strong> if it\nhas <strong>at least one</strong> upper bound, <strong>bounded\nbelow</strong> if it has at least one lower bound, and\n<strong>bounded</strong> if it is both bounded above and bounded\nbelow.</p>","file":"ch01-least-upper-bound/02-suprema.html"}